---
description: Apply Qodo coding rules before edits, and use Qodo for local review and posted pull request findings.
alwaysApply: true
---

This plugin connects Qodo through its skills and the `qodo-managed-tools` MCP server.

- Before implementing, editing, or refactoring, use `qodo-get-rules`. Reuse rules already loaded for the same repository and task. Treat ERROR rules as requirements. Treat WARNING and RECOMMENDATION rules as advisory.
- Use `qodo-review` at a substantive milestone and before handing off completed work. Skip trivial edits.
- Use `qodo-review-resolver` when the user wants posted Qodo pull request findings fixed.
- Use `qodo-codebase-wisdom` when the question is how this codebase is structured.
- If Qodo is not connected and the user asked to set it up, use `qodo-setup`. Otherwise continue, and say that Qodo was not applied.

Follow each skill's own transport instructions. `qodo-get-rules` uses the connected `rules-search` tool when that tool is present. `qodo-review` uses the `qodo` CLI when it is installed, because the CLI collects the working tree.
